Install:
    tested on python=3.10, CUDA=12.1, pytorch=2.6

    pip install torch=2.6 torchvision=0.21 torchaudio=2.6
    pip install -re requirements.txt
    pip install -e .

    cd HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget
    git checkout g1_hri_mllm(maybe not need this line?)
    pip install -e .

Compute joint_vec for g1ml3d:
    python HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget/HRI_retarget/scripts/g1ml3d_motion_representation.py 
    python HRI_mllm/external/HRI_retarget/HRI_retarget/utils/io/humanml3d_mean_variance.py
    copy texts folder


Train motion VQVAE:
    python HRI_mllm/train/train_vae.py


VQVAE:
    python HRI_mllm/scripts/test_motion_encoder.py



Train motion adaptor:
    generate motion tokens first:
        python HRI_mllm/scripts/generate_motion_tokens.py

    then 
        python -m torch.distributed.launch --nproc_per_node=8 --nnodes=1 --node_rank=0 \
            HRI_mllm/train/train_motion_adaptor.py \


Inference with gpt2 motion adaptor:
    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 python HRI_mllm/scripts/test_qwen2_5omni_motion_full.py 


Server:
    python HRI_mllm/inference/text_response_server.py

    # visit http://localhost:5000/response?text=your_text_here

    # or use curl
    # curl -X GET "http://localhost:5000/response?text=your_text_here"



